#: data/nation/conch.ruleset:3
msgid "Conch"
msgstr "conchrepublikanska"

#: data/nation/conch.ruleset:4
msgid "?plural:Conch"
msgstr "conchrepublikanerna"

#: data/nation/conch.ruleset:6
msgid ""
"In 1982, as part of a protest to a US Border Patrol station near Monroe "
"County, Florida, the city of Key West declared that they were seceding from "
"the US as the Conch Republic. They then declared war against the US, by "
"breaking a loaf of stale Cuban bread over the head of a man dressed as a "
"sailor. They surrendered after one minute, and then requested one billion "
"dollars of foreign aid. The faux-secession of the Conch Republic helped "
"bring awareness to issues of the Florida Keys, and the border patrol station "
"was quietly removed. To this day, Key West sells Conch Republic memorabilia "
"to tourists, and the Conch Republic has been involved in other protests by "
"Key West and the Florida Keys."
msgstr ""
"År 1982 utropade staden Key West i Florida sitt utträde ur USA under namnet "
"Conchrepubliken, i protest mot den amerikanska gränspolisens kontrollstation "
"nära Monroe County. Republiken förklarade sedan krig mot USA genom att "
"knäcka en gammal kubansk brödlimpa mot huvudet på en man utklädd till "
"matros. Efter en minut kapitulerade republiken och begärde därefter en "
"miljard dollar i bistånd. Låtsasrepublikens utträde drog uppmärksamhet till "
"problemen i Florida Keys, och gränspolisens kontrollstation avlägsnades i "
"tysthet. I Key West säljs fortfarande souvenirer från Conchrepubliken till "
"turister, och republiken har deltagit i andra protester i Key West och "
"övriga Florida Keys."

#: data/nation/confederate.ruleset:3
msgid "Confederate"
msgstr "sydstatska"

#: data/nation/confederate.ruleset:4
msgid "?plural:Confederates"
msgstr "sydstatarna"

#: data/nation/confederate.ruleset:6
msgid ""
"The Confederate States of America was a splinter nation of the United "
"States, formed by eleven Southern states, existing from 1861 to 1865. The "
"states seceded from the United States because of political and cultural "
"differences with the North, most prominently the issue of slavery, which "
"they feared the government of the recently elected United States president "
"Abraham Lincoln would abolish. The Confederate capital was Richmond, "
"Virginia, and Jefferson Davis was the country's only president. The American "
"Civil War pitted the Confederacy against the United States. After several "
"military defeats by United States troops the southern states had to abandon "
"their claims of independence; much of their territory laid in ruins. "
"Furthermore, the Union victory in the Civil War opened the way for the "
"abolition of slavery in the United States."
msgstr ""
"Amerikas konfedererade stater var en utbrytarstat som bildades av elva av "
"USA:s sydstater och existerade 1861–1865. Staterna lämnade USA på grund av "
"politiska och kulturella motsättningar med nordstaterna. Framför allt gällde "
"det slaveriet, som de fruktade att den nyvalde presidenten Abraham Lincolns "
"regering skulle avskaffa. Konfederationens huvudstad var Richmond i "
"Virginia, och Jefferson Davis var dess ende president. Under det amerikanska "
"inbördeskriget stred konfederationen mot USA. Efter flera militära nederlag "
"mot unionens trupper tvingades sydstaterna ge upp sina anspråk på "
"självständighet. Stora delar av deras territorium låg i ruiner. Unionens "
"seger i inbördeskriget banade också väg för att slaveriet avskaffades i USA."

#: data/nation/congolesebrazzaville.ruleset:3
msgid "Brazzaville-Congolese"
msgstr "brazzavillekongolesiska"

#: data/nation/congolesebrazzaville.ruleset:4
msgid "?plural:Brazzaville-Congolese"
msgstr "brazzavillekongoleserna"

#: data/nation/congolesebrazzaville.ruleset:6
msgid ""
"The Republic of the Congo is a country in Central Africa, not to be confused "
"with the Democratic Republic of the Congo. Congo has been independent from "
"France since 1960. From 1970 to 1991 it was governed as a Marxist-Leninist "
"one party state; in this period the country was known as the People's "
"Republic of the Congo. The country's economy relies heavily on the export of "
"petroleum."
msgstr ""
"Republiken Kongo, eller Kongo-Brazzaville, ligger i Centralafrika och är ett "
"annat land än Demokratiska republiken Kongo. Landet blev självständigt från "
"Frankrike 1960. Från 1970 till 1991 styrdes det som en marxist-leninistisk "
"enpartistat och hette då Folkrepubliken Kongo. Landets ekonomi är starkt "
"beroende av oljeexporten."

#: data/nation/congolese.ruleset:3
msgid "Congolese"
msgstr "kongolesiska"

#: data/nation/congolese.ruleset:4
msgid "?plural:Congolese"
msgstr "kongoleserna"

#: data/nation/congolese.ruleset:7
msgid ""
"The Democratic Republic of the Congo is a big country in Central Africa. "
"Despite (or because of) its wealth of natural resources it has been in ruins "
"for most of its modern history. In 1885 Congo was awarded to Léopold II of "
"Belgium as his personal possession, the Congo Free State, which turned the "
"country into a slaughterhouse. At least twenty per cent of the population "
"perished and after an international outcry it became a Belgian colony in "
"1906. It achieved independence in 1960. The Mobutu dictatorship started a "
"new round of pillaging. When Mobutu was toppled the country sank into a "
"civil war, causing five million deaths, the bloodiest event since World War "
"II."
msgstr ""
"Demokratiska republiken Kongo är ett stort land i Centralafrika. Trots sina "
"rika naturtillgångar, eller kanske på grund av dem, har landet legat i "
"ruiner under en stor del av sin moderna historia. År 1885 tilldelades "
"Belgiens kung Leopold II Kongo som sin personliga besittning under namnet "
"Kongofristaten. Under hans styre blev massmord en del av vardagen. Minst en "
"femtedel av befolkningen dog, och efter internationella protester blev Kongo "
"en belgisk koloni 1906. Landet blev självständigt 1960. Under Mobutus "
"diktatur inleddes en ny omgång plundring. När Mobutu störtades sjönk landet "
"ned i ett inbördeskrig som krävde fem miljoner liv och blev den blodigaste "
"händelsen sedan andra världskriget."

# ?
#: data/nation/cornish.ruleset:3
msgid "Cornish"
msgstr "korniska"

# ?
#: data/nation/cornish.ruleset:4
msgid "?plural:Cornish"
msgstr "kornierna"

#: data/nation/cornish.ruleset:6
msgid ""
"Cornwall is a region in the extreme southwest of England, traditionally the "
"home of the legendary King Arthur."
msgstr ""
"Cornwall är en region längst ned i sydvästra England och var enligt sägnen "
"kung Arturs hemland."

#: data/nation/corsican.ruleset:3
msgid "Corsican"
msgstr "korsikanska"

#: data/nation/corsican.ruleset:4
msgid "?plural:Corsicans"
msgstr "korsikanerna"

#: data/nation/corsican.ruleset:6
msgid ""
"For most of its history, Corsica has been ruled by foreign powers. Greeks, "
"Etruscans, Romans, Vandals, Visigoths, Byzantines, Saracens, Lombards, the "
"Papal States and Genoese all held sway over Corsica at one time or another. "
"The 18th century saw a war of independence inspired by Enlightenment values. "
"Pasquale Paoli managed to kick out the Genoese and from 1755 to 1769 Corsica "
"was an independent republic with the first modern constitution in the world. "
"Genoa sold its claim to France, after which a French invasion force defeated "
"the Corsicans and Corsica was incorporated into France."
msgstr ""
"Under större delen av sin historia har Korsika styrts av främmande makter. "
"Vid olika tider har greker, etrusker, romare, vandaler, visigoter, "
"bysantiner, saracener, langobarder, Kyrkostaten och Genua alla härskat över "
"ön. På 1700-talet utkämpades ett självständighetskrig inspirerat av "
"upplysningens idéer. Pasquale Paoli lyckades fördriva genuesarna. Från 1755 "
"till 1769 var Korsika en självständig republik med världens första moderna "
"författning. Genua sålde sina anspråk på ön till Frankrike. En fransk "
"invasionsstyrka besegrade sedan korsikanerna och Korsika införlivades med "
"Frankrike."

#: data/nation/corsican.ruleset:32
#, c-format
msgid "General-in-Chief %s"
msgstr "Överbefälhavare %s"

#: data/nation/corsican.ruleset:32
#, c-format
msgid "?female:General-in-Chief %s"
msgstr "Överbefälhavare %s"

#: data/nation/cossack.ruleset:3
msgid "Cossack"
msgstr "kosackiska"

#: data/nation/cossack.ruleset:4
msgid "?plural:Cossacks"
msgstr "kosackerna"

#: data/nation/cossack.ruleset:6
msgid ""
"The Zaporozhian Cossacks lived in Zaporozhia, in Central Ukraine. They were "
"a multi-ethnic community with Ruthenians being the dominant element, "
"organized in a military manner."
msgstr ""
"Zaporizjzjakosackerna levde i Zaporizjzja i centrala Ukraina. De utgjorde "
"ett militärt organiserat samhälle med flera folkgrupper, där rutenerna var "
"den dominerande gruppen."

#: data/nation/cossack.ruleset:31 data/nation/donetsk.ruleset:42
#: data/nation/lipkatatar.ruleset:29 data/nation/luhansk.ruleset:39
#: data/nation/ukrainian.ruleset:39
#, c-format
msgid "Hetman %s"
msgstr "Hetman %s"

#: data/nation/cossack.ruleset:31 data/nation/donetsk.ruleset:42
#: data/nation/lipkatatar.ruleset:29 data/nation/luhansk.ruleset:39
#: data/nation/ukrainian.ruleset:39
#, c-format
msgid "?female:Hetman %s"
msgstr "Hetman %s"

#: data/nation/costarican.ruleset:3
msgid "Costa Rican"
msgstr "costaricanska"

#: data/nation/costarican.ruleset:4
msgid "?plural:Costa Ricans"
msgstr "costaricanerna"

#: data/nation/costarican.ruleset:6
msgid ""
"Costa Rica became an independent republic in 1840. It has been without an "
"army since 1949 and is one of the most democratic and wealthy countries of "
"Latin America."
msgstr ""
"Costa Rica blev en självständig republik 1840. Landet har saknat armé sedan "
"1949 och är ett av Latinamerikas mest demokratiska och välmående länder."

#: data/nation/cree.ruleset:3
msgid "Cree"
msgstr "creeiska"

#: data/nation/cree.ruleset:4
msgid "?plural:Cree"
msgstr "creefolket"

#: data/nation/cree.ruleset:7
msgid ""
"The Cree are the largest native group in Canada with over 200,000 members "
"who speak an Algonquian language and often call themselves \"Iiyiyuu\" or "
"\"Iinuu,\" meaning \"people.\" They originally inhabited much of Quebec, "
"Labrador, Alberta, Saskatchewan, Ontario and Manitoba."
msgstr ""
"Cree är Kanadas största urfolk med över 200 000 medlemmar. De talar ett "
"algonkinspråk och kallar sig ofta iiyiyuu eller iinuu, vilket betyder "
"”folk”. De bebodde ursprungligen stora delar av Québec, Labrador, Alberta, "
"Saskatchewan, Ontario och Manitoba."

#: data/nation/cretan.ruleset:3
msgid "Cretan"
msgstr "kretensiska"

#: data/nation/cretan.ruleset:4
msgid "?plural:Cretans"
msgstr "kretensarna"

#: data/nation/cretan.ruleset:6
msgid ""
"Crete is an island in the Mediterranean Sea, the largest of the Greek "
"Archipelago. In the 3rd and 2nd millennia BCE Crete was the site of Europe's "
"first advanced civilization, the Minoan culture. An eruption of nearby Thera "
"destroyed the Minoan civilization. Crete then became part of the Greek "
"cultural realm, and was subsequently conquered by the Romans, Arabs, "
"Byzantines, Venetians and Ottoman Turks. After having been a semi-"
"independent state for 15 years, Crete finally became part of Greece in 1913."
msgstr ""
"Kreta ligger i Medelhavet och är den största ön i den grekiska övärlden. "
"Under tredje och andra årtusendet f.Kr. var Kreta hem för Europas första "
"högkultur, den minoiska kulturen. Ett vulkanutbrott på den närbelägna ön "
"Thera förstörde den minoiska civilisationen. Därefter blev Kreta en del av "
"den grekiska kulturkretsen och erövrades i tur och ordning av romare, "
"araber, bysantiner, venetianare och osmanska turkar. Efter 15 år som delvis "
"självständig stat blev Kreta slutligen en del av Grekland 1913."

#: data/nation/crimeantatar.ruleset:3
msgid "Crimean Tatar"
msgstr "krimtatariska"

#: data/nation/crimeantatar.ruleset:4
msgid "?plural:Crimean Tatars"
msgstr "krimtatarerna"

#: data/nation/crimeantatar.ruleset:6
msgid ""
"Historical feudal state on the Crimean Peninsula, existing from the 15th to "
"the 18th century. Crimean Tatars invaded Poland and Russia, which caused "
"wars with Turkey."
msgstr ""
"En feodalstat på Krimhalvön som fanns från 1400-talet till 1700-talet. "
"Krimtatarernas invasioner av Polen och Ryssland ledde till krig med Turkiet."

#: data/nation/croatian.ruleset:3
msgid "Croatian"
msgstr "kroatiska"

#: data/nation/croatian.ruleset:4
msgid "?plural:Croatians"
msgstr "kroaterna"

#: data/nation/croatian.ruleset:6
msgid ""
"Croatia is a country in Southeast Europe. In the 7th century they migrated "
"into the region and established a duchy which evolved to a kingdom in the "
"10th century under Tomislav. After the Trpimirović dynasty followed a period "
"of symbiotic regimes with varying foreign powers, mostly notably with "
"Austria-Hungary and the Ottoman Empire. In 1918, Croatia proclaimed "
"independence from Austria-Hungary alongside other Southeast European "
"nations. In World War II, the Axis installed a fascist puppet government "
"that was later dismantled by resistance. Croatia was a member state of the "
"newfound Yugoslav Federation until 1991 when they proclaimed independence "
"leading to four years long conflict resulting in Croatia securing its "
"autonomy."
msgstr ""
"Kroatien ligger i sydöstra Europa. Kroaterna invandrade till området på 600-"
"talet och grundade ett hertigdöme som under Tomislav på 900-talet blev ett "
"kungarike. Efter dynastin Trpimirović följde en tid då landets styre på "
"olika sätt var knutet till främmande makter, främst Österrike-Ungern och "
"Osmanska riket. År 1918 förklarade sig Kroatien självständigt från Österrike-"
"Ungern tillsammans med andra sydösteuropeiska nationer. Under andra "
"världskriget tillsatte axelmakterna en fascistisk marionettregering som "
"senare störtades av motståndsrörelsen. Kroatien blev en delrepublik i den "
"nybildade jugoslaviska federationen och förblev det fram till "
"självständighetsförklaringen 1991. En fyra år lång konflikt följde innan "
"Kroatien hade säkrat sitt självstyre."

#: data/nation/crusader.ruleset:3
msgid "Crusader"
msgstr "korsfararnas"

#: data/nation/crusader.ruleset:4
msgid "?plural:Crusaders"
msgstr "korsfararna"

#: data/nation/crusader.ruleset:6
msgid ""
"The Crusades were a series of wars in which European armies tried to re-"
"establish Christian control over the Holy Land. The First Crusade was called "
"by Pope Urban II in 1095. The crusaders managed to wrestle control of much "
"of the Levant from Muslim hands and established a number of states led by "
"noblemen from European Christian dynasties. The most powerful of crusader "
"states was the Kingdom of Jerusalem; other states included the County of "
"Tripoli, the Principality of Antioch and the Country of Edessa. Later "
"crusades were less successful. Muslim (Arab and Turkic) armies managed to "
"push back the Crusaders and the last Crusader controlled city, Acre, fell to "
"the Mamluks in 1291."
msgstr ""
"Korstågen var en serie krig där europeiska härar försökte återupprätta "
"kristet styre över det heliga landet. Påven Urban II uppmanade till det "
"första korståget 1095. Korsfararna erövrade stora delar av Levanten från "
"muslimska härskare och grundade flera stater ledda av adelsmän från "
"europeiska kristna dynastier. Kungariket Jerusalem var den mäktigaste "
"korsfararstaten. Bland de andra fanns grevskapet Tripoli, furstendömet "
"Antiochia och grevskapet Edessa. Senare korståg var mindre framgångsrika. "
"Muslimska härar av araber och turkfolk drev tillbaka korsfararna, och år "
"1291 erövrade mamlukerna den sista staden under korsfararnas kontroll, Akko."

#: data/nation/cuban.ruleset:3
msgid "Cuban"
msgstr "kubanska"

#: data/nation/cuban.ruleset:4
msgid "?plural:Cubans"
msgstr "kubanerna"

#: data/nation/cuban.ruleset:6
msgid ""
"Cuba came under Spanish control in the 16th century. In the following "
"centuries, the island became one of the leading producers of tobacco, sugar "
"and coffee in the world. Cuba was granted nominal independence in 1902."
msgstr ""
"Kuba kom under spanskt styre på 1500-talet. Under de följande århundradena "
"blev ön en av världens ledande producenter av tobak, socker och kaffe. Kuba "
"fick formell självständighet 1902."

#: data/nation/curonian.ruleset:3
msgid "Curonian"
msgstr "kurländska"

#: data/nation/curonian.ruleset:4
msgid "?plural:Curonians"
msgstr "kurländarna"

#: data/nation/curonian.ruleset:6
msgid ""
"The Duchy of Courland and Semigallia was created as the result of the "
"secularization of the Teutonic Order State. The dukes of Courland were "
"vassals of Poland until its collapse. Duke Jakob Kettler led the failed "
"attempts of colonization in South America and Africa."
msgstr ""
"Hertigdömet Kurland och Semgallen uppstod när Tyska ordens stat "
"sekulariserades. Hertigarna av Kurland var vasaller under Polen fram till "
"den polska statens sammanbrott. Hertig Jakob Kettler ledde misslyckade "
"kolonisationsförsök i Sydamerika och Afrika."

#: data/nation/cuyavian.ruleset:3
msgid "Cuyavian"
msgstr "kujaviska"

#: data/nation/cuyavian.ruleset:4
msgid "?plural:Cuyavians"
msgstr "kujavierna"

#: data/nation/cuyavian.ruleset:6
msgid ""
"Cuyavia is a historical region in Northern-Central Poland, bordered to the "
"East by Masovia, on the West by Greater Poland and on the North by Pomerania."
msgstr ""
"Kujavien är en historisk region i norra delen av centrala Polen. Det gränsar "
"i öster till Masovien, i väster till Storpolen och i norr till Pommern."

#: data/nation/cypriot.ruleset:3
msgid "Cypriot"
msgstr "cypriotiska"

#: data/nation/cypriot.ruleset:4
msgid "?plural:Cypriots"
msgstr "cyprioterna"

#: data/nation/cypriot.ruleset:6
msgid ""
"Cyprus became an independent republic on 16th August 1960. It is a Eurasian "
"island country located in the eastern Mediterranean, south of Turkey and "
"west of Syria and Lebanon."
msgstr ""
"Cypern blev en självständig republik den 16 augusti 1960. Det är en eurasisk "
"önation i östra Medelhavet, söder om Turkiet och väster om Syrien och "
"Libanon."

#: data/nation/cyrenaican.ruleset:3
msgid "Cyrenaican"
msgstr "kyrenaiska"

#: data/nation/cyrenaican.ruleset:4
msgid "?plural:Cyrenaicans"
msgstr "kyrenaikerna"

#: data/nation/cyrenaican.ruleset:6
msgid ""
"Cyrenaica is a historical region in Eastern Libya. In Classical Antiquity "
"the region was part of the Greek cultural realm. From the 7th century "
"onwards the region was controlled by various Arab dynasties. Cyrenaica was "
"occupied by Italy in 1911. After World War II a short-lived Emirate of "
"Cyrenaica existed, of which the ruling Senussi dynasty established a united "
"Libyan Kingdom in 1951. Cyrenaica has been a hotbed of resistance against "
"the Gaddafi regime. The site of much of Libya's oil reserves, Cyrenaica has "
"seen renewed calls for autonomy following the overthrow of Gaddafi."
msgstr ""
"Kyrenaika är en historisk region i östra Libyen. Under antiken tillhörde den "
"den grekiska kulturkretsen. Från 600-talet styrdes den av olika arabiska "
"dynastier. Italien ockuperade Kyrenaika 1911. Efter andra världskriget fanns "
"där under en kort tid ett emirat, vars härskande senussidynasti bildade ett "
"enat libyskt kungarike 1951. Kyrenaika var ett starkt fäste för motståndet "
"mot Gaddafiregimen. Regionen har en stor del av Libyens oljereserver, och "
"efter att Gaddafi störtades har kraven på självstyre åter tagit fart."

#: data/nation/czechoslovak.ruleset:3
msgid "Czechoslovakian"
msgstr "tjeckoslovakiska"

#: data/nation/czechoslovak.ruleset:4
msgid "?plural:Czechoslovakians"
msgstr "tjeckoslovakerna"

#: data/nation/czechoslovak.ruleset:6
msgid ""
"Czechoslovakia was founded in 1918. It was long the only democracy in "
"Eastern Europe until it was overrun by the Nazis in 1939 and the Soviet "
"Union in 1948. Four years after the fall of communism it was split into the "
"Czech and Slovak republics."
msgstr ""
"Tjeckoslovakien grundades 1918. Landet var länge den enda demokratin i "
"Östeuropa. År 1939 tog nazisterna över och 1948 tog Sovjetunionen makten. "
"Fyra år efter kommunismens fall delades landet i Tjeckien och Slovakien."

#: data/nation/czech.ruleset:3
msgid "Czech"
msgstr "tjeckiska"

#: data/nation/czech.ruleset:4
msgid "?plural:Czechs"
msgstr "tjeckerna"

#: data/nation/czech.ruleset:6
msgid ""
"Today's Czech Republic was until 1993 part of Czechoslovakia, which had been "
"until 1918 part of the Austro-Hungarian Empire."
msgstr ""
"Dagens Tjeckien var fram till 1993 en del av Tjeckoslovakien. Fram till 1918 "
"tillhörde området Österrike-Ungern."

#: data/nation/czech.ruleset:34 data/nation/xhosa.ruleset:27
#, c-format
msgid "Prophet %s"
msgstr "Profeten %s"

#: data/nation/czech.ruleset:34 data/nation/moravian.ruleset:35
#: data/nation/xhosa.ruleset:27
#, c-format
msgid "Prophetess %s"
msgstr "Profetissan %s"

#: data/nation/dacian.ruleset:3
msgid "Dacian"
msgstr "dakiska"

#: data/nation/dacian.ruleset:4
msgid "?plural:Dacians"
msgstr "dakerna"

#: data/nation/dacian.ruleset:6
msgid ""
"The Dacians were ancient tribes who lived on the left bank of the Lower "
"Danube in Dacia in what is now Romania. They were probably related to the "
"Thracians and other Paleo-Balkanic tribes. The unification of Dacian tribes "
"occurred during the reign of king Burebista. After the wars with Rome, they "
"were defeated in 106 CE. Dacia became a Roman province and succumbed to "
"Roman colonization. The remains of the Dacians mingled with East Germanic "
"tribes and later with Slavs."
msgstr ""
"Dakerna var forntida stammar som levde på nedre Donaus vänstra strand i "
"Dakien, i nuvarande Rumänien. De var troligen besläktade med thrakerna och "
"andra forntida folk på Balkan. De dakiska stammarna enades under kung "
"Burebistas regeringstid. Efter krig mot Rom besegrades de år 106 e.Kr. "
"Dakien blev en romersk provins och koloniserades av romarna. De återstående "
"dakerna blandades med östgermanska stammar och senare med slaver."

#: data/nation/dagestan.ruleset:3
msgid "Dagestan"
msgstr "dagestanska"

#: data/nation/dagestan.ruleset:4
msgid "?plural:Dagestani"
msgstr "dagestanierna"

#: data/nation/dagestan.ruleset:7
msgid ""
"Dagestan is a republic of Russia situated in North Caucausus along the "
"Caspian sea, it is one of the most ethnically diverse of Russia's republics, "
"it was one of the first people within the modern borders of Russia to become "
"Muslims after the Arab conquest of the region in 643. Dagestan was later "
"raided by the Mongols in 1221. Dagestan eventually came under the control of "
"Russia in 1813 and was firmly in the control of Imperial Russia as of 1828. "
"Due to high taxation and general dissatisfaction with the Russian "
"government, it rose up multiple times against Russia, once in 1828, and "
"again in 1917, it eventually became an autonomous republic under the Soviet "
"Union in 1921."
msgstr ""
"Dagestan är en delrepublik i Ryssland vid Kaspiska havet i norra Kaukasien. "
"Det är en av de ryska delrepubliker som har störst etnisk mångfald. Efter "
"den arabiska erövringen 643 var invånarna bland de första inom dagens ryska "
"gränser som övergick till islam. Mongolerna härjade i Dagestan 1221. År 1813 "
"kom området under rysk kontroll och 1828 hade det ryska imperiet befäst sitt "
"grepp om det. Höga skatter och allmänt missnöje med det ryska styret ledde "
"till flera uppror, bland annat 1828 och 1917. År 1921 blev Dagestan en "
"autonom republik under sovjetstyre."

#: data/nation/dahomean.ruleset:3
msgid "Dahomean"
msgstr "dahomeiska"

#: data/nation/dahomean.ruleset:4
msgid "?plural:Dahomeans"
msgstr "dahoméerna"

#: data/nation/dahomean.ruleset:6
msgid ""
"The southern third of modern Benin was once a historic kingdom known "
"variously as Agbome (c. 1600 - c. 1700), Danhome (c. 1700 - 1730), and "
"Dahomey (1730 - 1894). In 1730 the country became a tributary of the "
"neighboring kingdom of Oyo. It was conquered by France in the second Franco-"
"Dahomean war (1892 - 1894) and was split into Agbome and Alada.  In the 18th "
"and 19th centuries Dahomey was known for its fierce ahosi (gbeto) warriors: "
"an army of women who were the king's official bodyguards and celibate wives."
msgstr ""
"Den södra tredjedelen av dagens Benin utgjorde en gång ett kungarike som "
"gick under namnen Agbome (omkring 1600–1700), Danhome (omkring 1700–1730) "
"och Dahomey (1730–1894). År 1730 blev landet tributskyldigt till grannriket "
"Oyo. Frankrike erövrade landet i det andra fransk-dahomeiska kriget (1892–"
"1894) och delade det i Agbome och Alada. Under 1700- och 1800-talen var "
"Dahomey känt för sina fruktade ahosikrigare (gbeto). Dessa kvinnor var "
"kungens officiella livvakter och hustrur och levde i celibat."

#: data/nation/darfuri.ruleset:3
msgid "Darfuri"
msgstr "darfuriska"

#: data/nation/darfuri.ruleset:4
msgid "?plural:Darfuris"
msgstr "darfurierna"

#: data/nation/darfuri.ruleset:7
msgid ""
"The Sultanate of Darfur was an eastern so-called Sahelian state that from "
"its location in the region just south of the Sahara benefited and prospered "
"from trans-Saharan trade. The region had previously been dominated by the "
"Daju and Tunjur ethnic groups, the latter of which is traditionally thought "
"to have introduced Islam to the region. By the 16th century CE an ethnic "
"group known as the Fur had gained the upper hand and under Sultan Sulayman "
"established a long-lasting sultanate. The word Darfur means the Land of the "
"Fur."
msgstr ""
"Sultanatet Darfur var ett av de östra rikena i Sahel. Läget strax söder om "
"Sahara gjorde att riket blomstrade tack vare handeln genom öknen. Tidigare "
"hade folken daju och tunjur dominerat området. Enligt traditionen var det "
"tunjur som förde islam dit. På 1500-talet hade furfolket övertaget och "
"grundade under sultan Sulayman ett långlivat sultanat. Darfur betyder "
"”furfolkets land”."

#: data/nation/djiboutian.ruleset:3
msgid "Djiboutian"
msgstr "djiboutiska"

#: data/nation/djiboutian.ruleset:4
msgid "?plural:Djiboutians"
msgstr "djiboutierna"

#: data/nation/djiboutian.ruleset:6
msgid ""
"Djibouti is one of the smallest countries of Africa, located on the Gulf of "
"Aden. It has been independent from France since 1977. Djibouti's main ethnic "
"groups are the Afar and the Somalis. The country has one of the hottest "
"climates in the world."
msgstr ""
"Djibouti ligger vid Adenviken och är ett av Afrikas minsta länder. Landet "
"blev självständigt från Frankrike 1977. De största folkgrupperna är afarer "
"och somalier. Djibouti har ett av världens hetaste klimat."

#: data/nation/dominicano.ruleset:3
msgid "Dominicano"
msgstr "dominikanska"

#: data/nation/dominicano.ruleset:4
msgid "?plural:Dominicanos"
msgstr "dominikanerna"

#: data/nation/dominicano.ruleset:6
msgid ""
"The Dominican Republic is located on the eastern two thirds of the Caribbean "
"island of Hispaniola. Its capital - Santo Domingo - became the first "
"permanent European settlement in the Americas when it was founded by "
"Bartholomew Columbus in 1498."
msgstr ""
"Dominikanska republiken ligger på de östra två tredjedelarna av den "
"karibiska ön Hispaniola. Huvudstaden Santo Domingo blev den första "
"permanenta europeiska bosättningen i Amerika när Bartolomé Columbus grundade "
"den 1498."

#: data/nation/dominican.ruleset:3
msgid "Dominican"
msgstr "dominikiska"

#: data/nation/dominican.ruleset:4
msgid "?plural:Dominicans"
msgstr "dominikerna"

#: data/nation/dominican.ruleset:6
msgid ""
"The island of Dominica was first sighted by Europeans, including Christopher "
"Columbus, in 1493. Legend has it that the island was named so since the day "
"of its first sighting was a Sunday. Officially the \"Commonwealth of "
"Dominica\", the country should not be confused with the Dominican Republic, "
"another Caribbean nation."
msgstr ""
"De första européerna som fick syn på ön Dominica kom dit 1493. Bland dem "
"fanns Christofer Columbus. Enligt legenden fick ön sitt namn för att det var "
"en söndag. Landets officiella namn är Samväldet Dominica. Det ska inte "
"förväxlas med Dominikanska republiken, som också ligger i Karibien."

#: data/nation/donetsk.ruleset:3
msgid "Donetsk"
msgstr "donetskska"

#: data/nation/donetsk.ruleset:4
msgid "?plural:Donchyani"
msgstr "donetskborna"

#: data/nation/donetsk.ruleset:6
msgid ""
"The Donetsk People's Republic is an unrecognised republic of Russia in the "
"occupied parts of eastern Ukraine's Donetsk Oblast, with its capital in "
"Donetsk. The DPR was created by Russian-backed aramilitaries in 2014, and it "
"initially operated as a breakaway state Until it was annexed by Russia in "
"2022. Following Ukraine's Revolution of Dignity in 2014, pro-Russian, "
"counter-revolutionary unrest erupted in the eastern part of the country. "
"Russia annexed Crimea from Ukraine, while the armed separatists seized "
"government buildings and proclaimed the Donetsk People's Republic and "
"Luhansk People's Republic as independent states. This sparked the war in "
"Donbas, part of the wider Russo-Ukrainian War. The DPR and LPR are sometimes "
"described as puppet states of Russia during this conflict. They received no "
"international recognition from United Nations member states before 2022. On "
"21 February 2022, Russia recognised the DPR and LPR as sovereign states. "
"Three days later, Russia launched a full-scale invasion of Ukraine, "
"partially under the pretext of protecting the republics. Russian forces "
"captured more of Donetsk Oblast, which became part of the DPR. In September "
"2022, Russia proclaimed the annexation of the DPR and other occupied "
"territories, following illegitimate referendums. The United Nations General "
"Assembly passed a resolution calling on countries not to recognise what it "
"called the \"attempted illegal annexation\" and demanded that Russia "
"\"immediately, completely and unconditionally withdraw.\""
msgstr ""
"Folkrepubliken Donetsk är en internationellt icke erkänd republik som "
"Ryssland gör anspråk på i de ockuperade delarna av Donetsk oblast i östra "
"Ukraina, med Donetsk som huvudstad. Ryskstödda paramilitära grupper bildade "
"folkrepubliken 2014. Den fungerade som en utbrytarstat tills Ryssland "
"förklarade den annekterad 2022. Efter värdighetsrevolutionen i Ukraina 2014 "
"bröt proryska, kontrarevolutionära oroligheter ut i landets östra delar. "
"Ryssland annekterade Krim från Ukraina, medan väpnade separatister intog "
"myndighetsbyggnader och utropade folkrepublikerna Donetsk och Luhansk till "
"självständiga stater. Detta utlöste kriget i Donbas, en del av det större "
"rysk-ukrainska kriget. De båda folkrepublikerna beskrivs ibland som ryska "
"lydstater under konflikten. Före 2022 hade inget medlemsland i FN erkänt "
"dem. Den 21 februari 2022 erkände Ryssland dem som suveräna stater. Tre "
"dagar senare inledde Ryssland en fullskalig invasion av Ukraina, delvis "
"under förevändningen att skydda republikerna. Ryska styrkor intog fler delar "
"av Donetsk oblast, som införlivades med folkrepubliken. I september 2022 "
"tillkännagav Ryssland att det annekterade folkrepubliken Donetsk och andra "
"ockuperade områden efter illegitima folkomröstningar. FN:s generalförsamling "
"antog en resolution som uppmanade länder att inte erkänna vad församlingen "
"kallade ett ”försök till olaglig annektering” och krävde att Ryssland "
"”omedelbart, fullständigt och villkorslöst drar sig tillbaka”."

#: data/nation/donetsk.ruleset:40 data/nation/luhansk.ruleset:37
#, c-format
msgid "Kremlin %s"
msgstr "Kremlledaren %s"

#: data/nation/donetsk.ruleset:40 data/nation/luhansk.ruleset:37
#, c-format
msgid "?female:Kremlin %s"
msgstr "Kremlledaren %s"

#: data/nation/dryad.ruleset:3
msgid "Dryad"
msgstr "dryadiska"

#: data/nation/dryad.ruleset:4
msgid "?plural:Dryads"
msgstr "dryaderna"

#: data/nation/dryad.ruleset:6
msgid ""
"Dryads are creatures of Greek myth; they are a type of nymph associated with "
"trees. Dryads were generally considered to be shy and long-lived. They are "
"usually female and are often depicted as beautiful young women."
msgstr ""
"Dryader är väsen i grekisk mytologi, ett slags nymfer som hör samman med "
"träd. De ansågs i allmänhet vara skygga och leva länge. De är vanligen av "
"kvinnligt kön och avbildas ofta som vackra unga kvinnor."

#: data/nation/eastgerman.ruleset:3
msgid "East German"
msgstr "östtyska"

#: data/nation/eastgerman.ruleset:4
msgid "?plural:East Germans"
msgstr "östtyskarna"

#: data/nation/eastgerman.ruleset:6
msgid ""
"The German Democratic Republic was founded in the Soviet Occupation Zone of "
"postwar Germany in 1949. It was part of the Soviet dominated eastern bloc "
"during the Cold War. The GDR was known for the Berlin Wall and its vast "
"internal security apparatus, the Stasi. In 1989 the communist regime "
"collapsed and one year later it was annexed to the Federal Republic of "
"Germany."
msgstr ""
"Tyska demokratiska republiken (DDR) grundades 1949 i den sovjetiska "
"ockupationszonen i efterkrigstidens Tyskland. Under kalla kriget ingick "
"landet i det sovjetdominerade östblocket. DDR var känt för Berlinmuren och "
"den omfattande säkerhetstjänsten Stasi. År 1989 föll kommunistregimen och "
"ett år senare införlivades landet med Förbundsrepubliken Tyskland."

